The '''United States presidential election of 2016''' was the 58th quadrennial [[United States presidential election|American presidential election]], held on Tuesday, November 8, 2016. The [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] ticket of businessman [[Donald Trump]] and Indiana Governor [[Mike Pence]] defeated the [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] ticket of former [[United States Secretary of State|Secretary of State]] [[Hillary Clinton]] and U.S. Senator from Virginia [[Tim Kaine]]. Trump is expected to [[Inauguration of Donald Trump|take office]] as the [[List of Presidents of the United States|45th President]], and Pence as the [[List of Vice Presidents of the United States|48th Vice President]], on January 20, 2017.

Voters selected members of the [[Electoral College (United States)|Electoral College]] in each state, in most cases by [[Plurality voting system|"winner-takes-all" plurality]]; those state electors in turn voted for a new [[President of the United States|president]] and [[Vice President of the United States|vice president]] on December 19, 2016. Trump obtained the required [[majority vote|majority]] to become [[President-elect of the United States]], winning 30 states with 306 ''pledged'' electors out of 538.{{efn|name=pledged}} His victory had been considered unlikely by most media forecasts. Clinton received about {{Formatnum: {{#expr: ({{Formatnum: <!-- CLINTON: --> 65,844,954 |R}} - {{Formatnum: <!-- TRUMP: --> 62,979,879 |R}}) / 1e6 round 1}}}} million more votes nationwide, {{Formatnum: {{#expr: 100 * ({{Formatnum: <!-- CLINTON: --> 65,844,954 |R}} - {{Formatnum: <!-- TRUMP: --> 62,979,879 |R}}) / {{Formatnum: <!-- TOTAL: --> 137,053,916 |R}} round 1}}}}% of the total cast.

