'''Donald John Trump, Sr.''' (born June 14, 1946) is an American business magnate, investor,<ref name="Jeff Cox">{{cite web | url=http://www.cnbc.com/id/44102433 | title=Trump Changes Gears, Now Buying Bluechip Stocks | publisher=CNBC | date=August 11, 2011 | accessdate=July 9, 2013 | author=Jeff Cox}}</ref> author, television personality, and [[Donald Trump presidential campaign, 2016|candidate for President of the United States]] in the [[United States presidential election, 2016|2016 presidential election]]. He is chairman and president of [[The Trump Organization]] and the founder of [[Trump Entertainment Resorts]]. Trump's career, branding efforts, lifestyle, and outspoken manner helped make him a celebrity for years, a status amplified by the success of his NBC reality show, ''[[The Apprentice (U.S. TV series)|The Apprentice]]''.

Trump is a son of [[Fred Trump]], a [[New York City]] real estate developer. He was strongly influenced by his father in choosing a career in real estate development.<ref name="bio">{{cite web|title=Donald(John) Trump biography|publisher=biography.com|url=http://www.biography.com/people/donald-trump-9511238| accessdate=2015-12-18}}</ref>  Trump worked for his father's firm, Elizabeth Trump & Son, while attending the [[Wharton School of the University of Pennsylvania]], and officially joined the company in 1968 upon graduation. In 1971, he was given control of the company, renaming it The Trump Organization. He remains a major figure in United States real estate and a media celebrity.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.forbes.com/pictures/mfl45lhfj/donald-trump-3/ | title=Donald Trump | work=Forbes | accessdate=December 17, 2015}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=http://fortune.com/2015/09/29/trump-forbes-net-worth/ | title=Donald Trump furious at Forbes for ‘embarrassing’ net worth valuation | work=Fortune | date=September 29, 2015 | accessdate=December 17, 2015 | author=Michal Addady}}</ref>

