'''''Star Wars''''' is an American [[epic film|epic]] [[space opera]] franchise consisting of a [[film series]] created by [[George Lucas]]. The film series has spawned a [[media franchise]] outside the film series called the [[Star Wars Expanded Universe|Expanded Universe]] including [[List of Star Wars books|books]], television series, [[Star Wars computer and video games|computer and video games]], and [[List of Star Wars comic books|comic books]]. These supplements to the film trilogies have resulted in significant development of the series' [[fictional universe]]. These media kept the franchise active in the interim between the film trilogies. The franchise portrays a universe which is in a galaxy that is described as far, far away. It commonly portrays [[Jedi]] as a representation of good, in conflict with the [[Sith]], their evil counterpart. Their weapon of choice, the [[lightsaber]], is commonly recognized in popular culture. The fictional universe also contains many themes, especially influences of [[Philosophy and religion in Star Wars|philosophy and religion]].

