'''Taylor Alison Swift''' (born December 13, 1989) is an American [[singer-songwriter]].<ref name="Rolling Stone">{{cite web|title=The 100 Greatest Songwriters of All Time|url=http://www.rollingstone.com/music/lists/100-greatest-songwriters#taylor-swift|accessdate=October 11, 2015}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last1=Vincent|first1=Alice|title=Taylor Swift at AMAs 2014: 'music is valuable'|url=http://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/music/music-news/11249535/Taylor-Swift-at-AMAs-2014-music-is-valuable.html|website=The Telegraph|accessdate=October 11, 2015|date=November 24, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last1=Wilson |first1=Carl|title=Contemplating Taylor Swift's Navel|url=http://www.slate.com/articles/arts/music_box/2014/10/taylor_swift_s_1989_reviewed_could_the_secret_to_the_pop_star_s_world_conquering.html|website=Slate|accessdate=October 11, 2015|date=October 29, 2014}}</ref> Raised in [[Wyomissing, Pennsylvania]], she moved to [[Nashville, Tennessee]], at the age of 14 to pursue a career in [[country music]]. She signed with the independent label [[Big Machine Records]] and became the youngest songwriter ever signed by the [[Sony/ATV Music Publishing|Sony/ATV Music publishing house]]. The release of Swift's [[Taylor Swift (album)|self-titled debut album]] in 2006 marked the start of her career as a country music singer. Her third single, "[[Our Song (Taylor Swift song)|Our Song]]," made her the youngest person to single-handedly write and perform a number-one song on the [[Hot Country Songs|Hot Country Songs chart]].

